    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "French traders and trappers named Lac du Flambeau, or Lake of the Torches, after the practice of harvesting fish by torchlight.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        15,
        16
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://lacduflambeauchamber.com/history/"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "The Treaty of La Pointe established the Lac du Flambeau reservation in 1854.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        25
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lac_du_Flambeau%2C_Wisconsin"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Logging began on the reservation in 1885, and the town soon hosted the largest lumber yard in Wisconsin.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
